if your business is on life support  today I'm gonna share with you the three  ways to save your business from failing  hi I'm Evan Carmichael  I believe in entrepreneurs and I  recently got a question for one of my  YouTube subscribers love you guys  anyhoo wrote in to say are you in a  small photography studio and it seems  that conventional advertising is not  working and I need to generate some  revenue fairly quickly to support my  lease I applied for loans but because I  have returned in a heart condition no  one is willing to give me the money out  of risk I might die what can I do to  save my shop this is a great question  Amy thank you so much for writing in I  feel the stress and the angst and the  despair and the genuine desire to want  to make this business work and so here  are the three bits of device that I  would have to help you save your company  number one is live within your means  this is a little bit of tough love but  if you can't afford the lease for your  business then maybe you shouldn't have a  shop one of the biggest mistakes that  most entrepreneurs make is they start  spending money before they're making  money  anybody can spend money the trick is to  find customers start making money and  start building a business around them  and then you expand when you can afford  to expand now losing a shop doesn't mean  you have to close your business you can  do what you probably should have done in  the start is out of your home start  small build a customer base get revenue  coming in make sure you can pay your  bills and then expand and the last thing  you want to do is take out a loan  because now if the business doesn't work  they're gonna come after your house so  cut back on your expenses and that may  mean losing the shop and go out and get  customers so that you have a profitable  business number two is pick a niche and  form alliances listen there are tons of  photographers there are tons and tons  and tons of photographers what makes you  different you've got to pick a niche  that you excel at that you love dealing  with these kinds of people and then  express it in every communication that  you put out there so if you're writing a  question to me I love this here you say  hey I'm a photographer and I specialize  in taking pictures of athletes that  gives me a lot more context to help you  because if you're just a general  photographer there's so much competition  and it's really hard to stand out so you  want to pick your niche  then form alliances with people who can  help you sell into that niche so an  example is a buddy of mine named Richard  who was a celebrity photographer he has  a website called you gotta love and he  specializes in photography for  celebrities he's worked with acts like  Lady gaga  and high-profile rappers and musicians  and then he forms alliances with people  who are already selling to those  musicians and celebrities who work with  music agents and he'll work with music  labels and who work with people who  represent these stars already they have  a big client pool that they can  potentially introduce him to and because  he is the expert in that field he's  likely to get the business so pick a  niche that you were really good at that  you really want to target these kinds of  customers and then go form alliances  with people who have complementary  products and services that can introduce  you to their clients and number three is  provide amazing service your service  based business and the number one way  the service based businesses grow is  through referrals you should be able to  build a three hundred thousand dollar  business just on your own and just  through referrals and that counts by  providing amazing service after somebody  does a photo shoot with you what extra  value can you bring them so that they  can't wait to go and tell their friends  about you as an example the guy who shot  my wedding was named Brian and he's got  a company called tarsi pix he went way  over and above what was expected of him  he came the day before the wedding and  took shots of the setup he came with us  throughout the whole day of the wedding  he took pictures not just of us but of  every single guest that came out to the  wedding and then he made baseball cards  for us personalized to each individual  who came to the wedding he went way way  way way way above what I expected from a  wedding photographer and as a result now  every time I know someone is getting  married I say you kind of go work with  Brian I even made a video thanking him  for his amazing work doing your job and  providing good pictures is not enough  you have to over-deliver like crazy so  they can't wait to go out and tell their  friends about you so live within your  means pick a niche and form alliances  and provide amazing service and belief  for those who are watching I love to  know  how you live within your means how you  got your business from the bootstraps up  and how you overcame those early  obstacles leave it in the comments below  share your story I'd love to hear and it  can also help inspire other people who  are going through that same problem and  if you like this video you want to see  more don't forget to subscribe to the  newsletter and the channel thank you for  watching I'll see you soon
 

